				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/professor-ritchie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2289046); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2289046&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608045324" alt="Professor Ritchie" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2289046)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/professor-ritchie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2289046); return false;" >Professor Ritchie</a></span> <span class="odate time_1445876875 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Oct 2015 16:27</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2397416">
									

<p>Your tenses seem to jump around a bit, not sure if that was intentional or not though and you have a few bits of dodgy grammar.</p>
<p>&quot;Saints don't have to look good. Ours definitely doesn't.&quot; should be &quot;saints don't have to look good. Our definitely don't&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;You clearly haven't seen him without the polish. We're all human inside after all, don't you agree? Even with all the costumes, we're all the same. Don't judge a book by it's cover, nor classify it by the title.&quot; I wasn't sure if this was a third person talking or the man with the gears? If it was the gear man he shouldn't be referring to himself in the third person as he doesn't do that at any other time as far as I saw.</p>
<p>Was this part of a series or a standalone?</p>

							</div>

								
					
